---
/**
 * The frame the two admin pages share, and the whole of the admin surface's furniture.
 *
 * [ADR 0002](../../../docs/adr/0002-no-admin-accounts.md) rules out an admin area: no
 * account, no login, no navigation, because there is nowhere to navigate to that is not
 * another signed link. The pages share the site's base styles (`styles/base.css`, inlined
 * like everywhere else), which is a look and not an admin UI. No script, and both forms still
 * submit with no CSS loaded.
 *
 * `lang="en"` and not `es`, unlike every other page on the platform. The Platform Admin is
 * "a role in the domain, not in the auth system" (`CONTEXT.md`) and is the maintainer who
 * reads this repository; `CONTEXT.md`'s *User-facing Spanish* table governs what adopters
 * and shelters read, and translating a one-person tool would invent a Spanish vocabulary for
 * concepts — evidence, method, entry — that the glossary has no words for. The mail this
 * surface causes to be sent to a *shelter* is es-VE, in `lib/verification/mail.ts`, which is
 * where the boundary between the two audiences actually falls.
 */
import "../styles/base.css";

interface Props {
  title: string;
  heading: string;
}

const { title, heading } = Astro.props;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title} — Pawster admin</title>
    <!--
      Never indexed, and here the reason is sharper than on the shelter pages: the URL that
      reaches this page carries a bearer capability in its query string, and a search engine
      that crawled one would hold the credential. `noindex` is not the defence — the
      capability's expiry is — but a crawler has no business here either way.
    -->
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <!--
      No referrer, because the token is in the URL. Any link this page renders to a shelter's
      own public page would otherwise hand that request's `Referer` header the admin's live
      capability, and the shelter's page is served by the same Worker that would log it.
    -->
    <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer" />
  </head>
  <body class="wrap">
    <h1>{heading}</h1>
    <slot />
  </body>
</html>
